{
  "note": "Rows from bank texts (docs/decisions/bank-texts.md, The op log). A text row is a v4 txn_ingested with entry_method mailbox, no provenance, no dedupe and no gates.ar, gates.sender trusted only when the sender matched the template's sms_sender, no gates.card (2026-10-29: filing has no card or sender check), and two keys that older builds ignore: channel \"sms\" and received_at (the arrival minute). Its ingest_id is an HMAC key (64 hex digits). The fold keeps channel and received_at on the row for the projection and leaves both out of the witness, so state_sha256 is what a build from before bank texts gives. A text row never forms the fold's implicit transfer pair (no gates.ar pass); the authoring side holds the second row of a DIB debit alert and transfer notice in Review instead, and the fold keeps both rows. A repeat with a new key inside ten minutes is a held probable copy; the same key again is duplicate_ingest; a repeat with no bank is a second row beside the first; an unparsed text row folds and accepts an archive. Every op is synthetic. Written by the Swift executor.",
